You are a visual design quality inspector. You will score how well an agent-generated webpage replicates the visual design of a reference page.

The FIRST image is the REFERENCE (ground truth).
The SECOND image is the AGENT-GENERATED version.

IMPORTANT: Do NOT evaluate text content — assume any differences in wording, numbers, or data are intentional. Focus entirely on visual design quality.

Score each of the five design dimensions below on a 1–5 scale. For each dimension, write one sentence explaining what you observed before giving the score.

CALIBRATION ANCHORS (apply to all dimensions):
- 5: essentially indistinguishable from reference — differences imperceptible without side-by-side comparison
- 4: minor issues only, would need close inspection to notice
- 3: clearly present but noticeably different from reference
- 2: significant problems, immediately obvious differences
- 1: completely wrong or absent

DIMENSIONS — look only at what is listed, ignore everything else:

1. color
   LOOK AT: brand accent colors on CTAs and buttons, gradient fills on hero/card elements, badge and pill background colors, icon colors, nav link colors
   IGNORE: large plain white/grey background areas

2. typography
   LOOK AT: heading font weight and size relative to body text, button and label font weight, badge/pill text styling (caps, weight, size), nav link font styling
   IGNORE: body paragraph and form field text content

3. assets
   LOOK AT: icon rendering (are icons displaying correctly or as boxes/placeholders?), emoji presence and rendering, decorative images, avatar or image placeholders, illustrations
   IGNORE: text content

4. proportion
   LOOK AT: button padding and overall size, pill/badge sizing, spacing between form elements and their labels, nav item density and spacing
   IGNORE: large empty whitespace areas between sections

5. states
   LOOK AT: selected/active pill or tab states, active or highlighted nav items, filled vs outline button variants, focused input styling, checked or toggled states on any interactive elements
   IGNORE: everything that is not an interactive element state

